\
Open data and code for the study \
\
The phonology of letter shapes: Feature economy and informativeness in 43 writing systems\
\
Yoolim Kim, Marc Allassonni\'e8re-Tang, Helena Miton, Olivier Morin\
\
This repository contains the data and code necessary to replicate the results we report in our paper. \
\
For all questions please email Olivier Morin : olivier.morin@ens.fr, alf.drummond@gmail.com\
\
For most files, a data dictionary (metadata text file) is given which explains their content.\
\
1. raw data: \
\
This folder contains all the data collected by us and others needed to run the code. \
The only exception is the Glottolog data which is accessible here: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7398962 \
(download the file languoid.csv).\
\
2. Code.R\
\
This R script contains all the code needed to replicate our results and generate the processed data, \
the results files, and the figures.\
\
3. processed data\
\
This folder contains the processed data generated from the raw data by the code, along with metadata files.\
All the data files it contains can be replicated using the code and raw data.\
\
4. Figures\
\
The data figures given in the paper, as generated from the code.\
\
